      "content": "The weight of shame and loss can feel suffocating, making it hard to imagine any kind of dignity left. It's like you're staring into the abyss, and all you can see is the mirror showing a stranger - a stranger who's broken and defeated. Take a deep breath and remember that dignity isn't about external validation or success; it's about being true to yourself, even when others might not see you as a whole person. Allow yourself to feel the emotions, but also hold on to a glimmer of self-respect, no matter how small it may seem.",
